{%- doc -%}
  Individual order detail (classic accounts). Rendered by templates/customers/order.liquid.
  Figma: Account_Dashboard_IndividualOrder (+ _Mobile). Layout = title + back/tracking row,
  then a foam card with an items TABLE (Product / SKU / Price / Quantity / Total) + order
  summary, then Billing Address and Shipping Address foam cards. Dashboard style tokens
  (foam cards #FEF8F3 r10, espresso text, Kurdis). Container matches the dashboard.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign card = 'rounded-[10px] bg-foam shadow-[0px_4px_4px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.25)]'

  # ---- QA preview -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # The real page needs a logged-in customer with an order, so the layout cannot be checked
  # locally. templates/search.order-preview.liquid renders this same section with mock values,
  # keyed off the global `template` (which carries the suffix) — no schema, no settings, and on
  # the real page `template` is "customers/order", so nothing below changes there.
  assign preview = false
  if template contains 'order-preview'
    assign preview = true
  endif

  if preview
    assign o_name = '#743463'
    assign o_placed_on = 'June 03, 2026'
    assign o_payment_status = 'Paid'
    assign o_fulfillment_status = 'Fulfilled'
    assign tracking_number = '435435'
    assign tracking_url = ''
    # title|sku|price|qty|total
    assign rows = '96OZ BUNDLE – 2 BOXES - 96OZ BUNDLE – 2 BOXES|staybundle|$0.00|1|$0.00;COLD BREW ON TAP (96 OZ) - BANANA BREAD - 2 BOX DISCOUNT PRICE|WBBB96oz|$34.99|1|$34.99;COLD BREW ON TAP (96 OZ) - ALMOND AMARETTO - 2 BOX DISCOUNT PRICE|WBAM96oz|$34.99|1|$34.99' | split: ';'
    assign o_subtotal = '$69.98'
    assign o_discount_title = 'TESTFreeQAAbsoluteWeb2236'
    assign o_discount = '-$10.00'
    assign o_shipping_label = 'Free Ground Shipping'
    assign o_shipping = '$0.00'
    assign o_total = '$69.98'
    assign o_billing = '2806 Via Alta Pl|San Diego|92108|United States' | split: '|'
    assign o_shipping_addr = '23972 Park Granada|Calabasas|91302|United States' | split: '|'
  else
    assign fulfillment = order.fulfillments.first
    assign tracking_number = fulfillment.tracking_number
    assign tracking_url = fulfillment.tracking_url
    assign o_name = order.name
    assign o_placed_on = order.created_at | date: '%B %d, %Y'
    assign o_payment_status = order.financial_status_label
    assign o_fulfillment_status = order.fulfillment_status_label
    assign rows = order.line_items
  endif
-%}

<section class="w-full" style="background-color: var(--color-brand-cream);">
  <div class="account-container py-8 md:!py-12">

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Title ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <h1 class="wb-order-title font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-espresso text-[25px] md:!text-[32px] leading-none">{{ 'customer.order.title' | t: name: o_name }}</h1>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Back link + Tracking Number ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} Back link and tracking number sit on one row side by side; on mobile there is
      not enough width for that, so .wb-order-head stacks them and centres both (account.css). {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} Stacked on mobile, so the gap is the space above the tracking line: 20px there,
      12px on the desktop row. Set on the class rather than in account.css because an unlayered
      !important cannot beat a Tailwind layered one. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wb-order-head flex items-center justify-between !gap-5 smd:!gap-3 mb-6">
      {%- comment -%} QA #14: hover feedback — same opacity pattern as .wb-redeem-btn.
        QA #22 (round 2): the arrow was a flex sibling, so it ate width from the label and the text
        sat right of the button centre. Arrow is now absolutely positioned and the label centres on
        the button itself. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} QA #22 asked for horizontal centring, and the arrow + label are centred as ONE
        group (confirmed with the client) — not the label alone. So the arrow stays a flex sibling
        and justify-center centres the pair; an absolutely positioned arrow would take the label to
        the button's centre and leave the visible group sitting left of it.
        This also lands on Figma 1:1162: a 14px arrow + 8px gap + the 107px label is 129px wide, so
        centring it in the 165px button puts the arrow 18px in from the edge, which is exactly the
        inset the frame specifies. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} The shared button (.btn + the blob shape, as rendered by snippets/wb-button),
        not a bespoke rounded rectangle: same silhouette, shadow and hover as every other CTA.
        Inlined rather than rendered through wb-button because that snippet emits a label span and
        nothing else, and this button also carries the arrow.
        secondary-cream, not secondary-gold: cream blob with espresso text at rest, inverting to a
        gold blob with cream text on hover. The two variants are exact mirrors of each other, so the
        direction is the style name alone — no per-button colour overrides either way.
        Sizing overrides .btn's own 205px width and 20px type; the height already matches at 43px. {%- endcomment -%}
      <a href="{{ routes.account_url }}" class="btn secondary-cream !w-[165px] !h-[43px] !text-[14px] !gap-2">
        {%- comment -%} The arrow sits in a <span> so it inherits .btn's span colour and its hover
          transition — as a bare child of the anchor it would keep the surrounding text colour and
          stay dark while the label turned cream. !static undoes `.btn svg { position: absolute;
          inset: 0 }`, which is meant for the blob and would otherwise stretch the arrow over the
          whole button; !fill-none undoes the blob's cream fill, which beats the element's own
          fill="none" attribute and would flood the open arrow path. {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="flex shrink-0"><svg class="!static !fill-none w-[14px] h-[10px]" viewBox="0 0 14 10" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 1 1 5l4 4M1 5h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
        {%- comment -%} QA: the label sat slightly high in Windows/Chrome. .wb-optical-center trims
          the text box to the glyphs so items-center lands on them, not on font metrics. {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="wb-optical-center">{{ 'customer.order.back_to_account' | t }}</span>
        <svg preserveAspectRatio="none" class="btn-svg w-full h-full drop-shadow-[4px_4px_4px_rgba(0,0,0,0.25)]" width="280" height="47" viewBox="0 0 280 47" fill="none">
          <path d="M2.59169 4.88727C0.390365 7.61342 0.302126 10.8262 0.264973 13.9059C0.176734 21.2351 0.09314 28.5613 0.00490134 35.8904C-0.0183194 37.8822 -0.0136752 39.9555 1.33777 41.7417C4.59331 46.0364 8.70337 46.9734 20.8617 46.9734C102.413 46.9734 183.968 47.1336 265.524 46.6681C268.418 46.653 271.594 46.7497 273.967 45.6707C280.399 42.7481 279.698 37.4077 279.503 33.4454C279.141 26.0678 280 20.005 280 12.6245C280 7.4623 279.113 5.38898 276.484 3.34587C273.117 0.725503 266.105 0.83733 260.852 0.767816C226.318 0.305398 191.766 0.0666329 157.218 0.0122307C122.448 -0.0451938 87.6769 0.0998786 52.9063 0.441403C43.0979 0.538118 33.2941 0.649945 23.4903 0.779905C16.0876 0.87662 6.6971 -0.187244 2.59169 4.88727Z"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
      {%- liquid
        assign tracking_class = 'font-gothic_condensed font-extrabold text-[16px] leading-none text-right underline text-espresso'
      -%}
      {%- if tracking_number -%}
        <a href="{{ tracking_url | default: '#' }}"{% if tracking_url %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %} class="{{ tracking_class }}">{{ 'customer.order.tracking_number' | t }}: {{ tracking_number }}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="{{ tracking_class }}">{{ 'customer.order.tracking_number' | t }}: {{ 'customer.order.tracking_pending' | t }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Card 1: order meta + items table + summary ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="{{ card }} p-5 md:!p-8 mb-6">
      {%- comment -%} QA #12: order-card body text is #1B1B1B (bear-black), matching the dashboard cards.
        QA #42: heavier — Figma has this table flattened into an image, so there is no weight to read
        off the frame; bumped a step by eye as agreed. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} font-bold is kept because .body.font-bold also carries the 16px size — dropping
        it would make this line smaller, not heavier. !font-extrabold then beats that rule's 700. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="body font-bold !font-extrabold text-bear-black">{{ 'customer.order.title' | t: name: o_name }}</div>
      {%- comment -%} Format the date BEFORE handing it to `t` — Liquid filters run left to right, so
        a trailing `| date` would be applied to the already-translated sentence, not to created_at. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[12px] leading-none text-bear-black mt-2 mb-6">{{ 'customer.order.placed_on' | t: date: o_placed_on }}</div>

      {%- comment -%} Desktop keeps the table. Below smd the five columns cannot share 350px — the
        product name shredded into six lines and the table scrolled sideways — so Figma 1:1301 drops
        the table entirely and stacks each item: title, SKU, unit price, then a Quantity / Total pair.
        Both presentations read the same normalised li_* values, so there is one source of truth for
        the data; only the markup differs. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="overflow-x-auto hidden smd:!block">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left">
          <thead>
            <tr class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[12px] uppercase text-bear-black align-bottom">
              <th class="font-bold pb-3 pr-4">{{ 'customer.order.col_product' | t }}</th>
              <th class="font-bold pb-3 px-4 whitespace-nowrap">{{ 'customer.order.col_sku' | t }}</th>
              <th class="font-bold pb-3 px-4 text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ 'customer.order.col_price' | t }}</th>
              <th class="font-bold pb-3 px-4 text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ 'customer.order.col_quantity' | t }}</th>
              <th class="font-bold pb-3 pl-4 text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ 'customer.order.total' | t }}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for row in rows -%}
              {%- liquid
                if preview
                  assign f = row | split: '|'
                  assign li_title = f[0]
                  assign li_sku = f[1]
                  assign li_price = f[2]
                  assign li_qty = f[3]
                  assign li_total = f[4]
                else
                  assign li_title = row.title
                  assign li_sku = row.sku
                  assign li_price = row.price | money
                  assign li_qty = row.quantity
                  assign li_total = row.final_line_price | money
                endif
              -%}
              <tr class="border-t border-espresso body text-bear-black align-top">
                {%- comment -%} QA #42: product title heavier than the rest of the row. {%- endcomment -%}
                <td class="py-4 pr-4 font-extrabold uppercase">{{ li_title }}</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4 whitespace-nowrap">{{ li_sku }}</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4 text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ li_price }}</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4 text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ li_qty }}</td>
                <td class="py-4 pl-4 text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ li_total }}</td>
              </tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Mobile: one block per line item (Figma 1:1301). {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="smd:!hidden body text-bear-black">
        {%- for row in rows -%}
          {%- liquid
            if preview
              assign f = row | split: '|'
              assign li_title = f[0]
              assign li_sku = f[1]
              assign li_price = f[2]
              assign li_qty = f[3]
              assign li_total = f[4]
            else
              assign li_title = row.title
              assign li_sku = row.sku
              assign li_price = row.price | money
              assign li_qty = row.quantity
              assign li_total = row.final_line_price | money
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="border-t border-espresso py-4">
            <div class="font-extrabold uppercase leading-[1.3]">{{ li_title }}</div>
            <div class="mt-2">{{ li_sku }}</div>
            <div class="mt-2">{{ 'customer.order.price_each' | t: price: li_price }}</div>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-baseline justify-between">
              <span>{{ 'customer.order.col_quantity' | t }}</span>
              <span>{{ 'customer.order.total' | t }}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
              <span>{{ li_qty }}</span>
              <span>{{ li_total }}</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

      {%- comment -%} Order summary (right-aligned) {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="border-t border-espresso pt-5 flex flex-col items-end !gap-4 body text-bear-black">
        {%- if preview -%}
          <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between"><span>{{ 'customer.order.subtotal' | t }}</span><span>{{ o_subtotal }}</span></div>
          <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between text-dark-gold"><span>{{ 'customer.order.discount' | t }} ({{ o_discount_title }})</span><span>{{ o_discount }}</span></div>
          <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between"><span>{{ o_shipping_label }}</span><span>{{ o_shipping }}</span></div>
          <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold"><span>{{ 'customer.order.total' | t }}</span><span>{{ o_total }}</span></div>
        {%- else -%}
        <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between"><span>{{ 'customer.order.subtotal' | t }}</span><span>{{ order.line_items_subtotal_price | money }}</span></div>
        {%- for discount in order.cart_level_discount_applications -%}
          <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between text-dark-gold"><span>{{ 'customer.order.discount' | t }} ({{ discount.title }})</span><span>-{{ discount.total_allocated_amount | money }}</span></div>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- comment -%} An order split across several delivery groups — a Stay AI bundle alongside
          ordinary line items, say — carries one shipping_method per group, which rendered as two
          identical "Free Ground Shipping $0.00" rows. When every method shares a title they collapse
          into one row carrying the order's total shipping. Genuinely different methods still list
          separately, so the summary never misreports what was charged. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign ship_titles = order.shipping_methods | map: 'title' | uniq -%}
        {%- if order.shipping_methods.size > 1 and ship_titles.size == 1 -%}
          <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between"><span>{{ ship_titles[0] }}</span><span>{{ order.shipping_price | money }}</span></div>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- for method in order.shipping_methods -%}
            <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between"><span>{{ method.title }}</span><span>{{ method.price | money }}</span></div>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between"><span>{{ 'customer.order.shipping' | t }}</span><span>{{ order.shipping_price | money }}</span></div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- for tax_line in order.tax_lines -%}
          <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between"><span>{{ 'customer.order.tax' | t }} ({{ tax_line.title }})</span><span>{{ tax_line.price | money }}</span></div>
        {%- endfor -%}
        <div class="flex w-full max-w-[360px] justify-between font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold"><span>{{ 'customer.order.total' | t }}</span><span>{{ order.total_price | money }}</span></div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Card 2: Billing Address ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="{{ card }} p-5 md:!p-8 mb-6">
      <h2 class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-bear-black text-[18px] leading-none mb-3">{{ 'customer.order.billing_address' | t }}</h2>
      {%- comment -%} QA #13: status line had no font class (system fallback) — Kurdis like the rest of the card. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-bear-black text-[16px] leading-[1.3] mb-6">{{ 'customer.order.payment_status' | t }}: {{ o_payment_status }}</div>
      {%- if preview -%}
        <address class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-bear-black not-italic">
          {{ o_billing[0] }}<br>{{ o_billing[1] }},<br>{{ o_billing[2] }} {{ o_billing[3] }}
        </address>
      {%- elsif order.billing_address -%}
        <address class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-bear-black not-italic">
          {{ order.billing_address.address1 }}<br>
          {%- if order.billing_address.address2 != blank %}{{ order.billing_address.address2 }}<br>{% endif -%}
          {{ order.billing_address.city }},<br>
          {{ order.billing_address.zip }} {{ order.billing_address.country }}
        </address>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Card 3: Shipping Address ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="{{ card }} p-5 md:!p-8">
      <h2 class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-bear-black text-[18px] leading-none mb-3">{{ 'customer.order.shipping_address' | t }}</h2>
      <div class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-bear-black text-[16px] leading-[1.3] mb-6">{{ 'customer.order.fulfillment_status' | t }}: {{ o_fulfillment_status }}</div>
      {%- if preview -%}
        <address class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-bear-black not-italic">
          {{ o_shipping_addr[0] }}<br>{{ o_shipping_addr[1] }},<br>{{ o_shipping_addr[2] }} {{ o_shipping_addr[3] }}
        </address>
      {%- elsif order.shipping_address -%}
        <address class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-bear-black not-italic">
          {{ order.shipping_address.address1 }}<br>
          {%- if order.shipping_address.address2 != blank %}{{ order.shipping_address.address2 }}<br>{% endif -%}
          {{ order.shipping_address.city }},<br>
          {{ order.shipping_address.zip }} {{ order.shipping_address.country }}
        </address>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
